      "inLanguage": "en",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What exactly is Galaxy Robot Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Galaxy Robot Park is Galaxy Corporation's theme park for experiencing AI with a body — Physical AI — first-hand. It is a place where AI that once lived inside phones and PCs takes on a robot's 'body' and actually dances and moves right in front of you. Built across roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) in Godeok, Gangdong District, Seoul, it is the first permanent stage where Galaxy Corporation's Physical AI and humanoid-robot technology comes to life as entertainment. The conceptual background is covered in the Physical AI whitepaper ."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where is Robot Park located?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It occupies roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) in Godeok, Gangdong District, Seoul. It is a dedicated Physical AI entertainment venue, separate from Galaxy Corporation's Three IFC headquarters in Yeouido. Precise location, transit and other visitor details follow Galaxy Corporation's official announcements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "When did it open? How does the pre-opening differ from the grand opening?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It first opened its doors for a pre-opening in July 2026, and held its grand opening (official launch) on August 21, 2026. The pre-opening was a roughly two-month preview window ahead of the official launch — a chance to see the robot shows and Physical AI experiences early. Every advance ticket sold out, and 20,000 visitors came through before the official opening. The grand opening added 17 new robots and a new interactive program in which visitors control the robots and engage with them directly, and brought the entire 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) site, food and beverage venues included, into full operation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What can you see at Robot Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The centerpiece is the 'K-pop Robot Arena.' Humanoid robots trained on real idol choreography perform group routines set to K-pop. Beyond that, there are robot boxing shows and interactive Physical AI experiences where visitors engage directly — a hugging robot, a robot dog and a drawing robot among them. What makes it a Physical AI theme park is that every piece of content plays out not on a screen but in real physical space, through the body of a robot."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How can a robot dance like an idol?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Humanoid robots learn real idol choreography from data and reproduce the group routines just as human dancers would. Learning human movement as data and expressing it through a robot's body — this is a signature application of Physical AI. Unlike AI that only answered questions on a screen, Physical AI actually moves in the physical world. The mechanics are covered in the Physical AI whitepaper and the Company core FAQ ."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Why put robots on a theme-park stage first, rather than on an industrial site?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Galaxy Corporation chose 'performance' as the setting where Physical AI first meets the public. A stage that moves people is the fastest proving ground for a robot's precision, safety and real-time interaction — and the surest path to making Physical AI part of everyday experience. This thinking is spelled out in the 'Why entertainment first' section of the Physical AI whitepaper ."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How will it operate after the official opening?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "After the official opening, the goal is to run the 'K-pop Robot Arena' show 4+ times a day, building a permanent performance system of 1,000+ shows a year. Unlike traditional performances that depend on an artist's physical schedule, Physical AI-driven robot shows can run continuously and on repeat."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do reservations and admission fees work?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The pre-opening ran on a reservation basis. Details for the period since the official opening — how to book, operating hours, admission fees and the like — follow Galaxy Corporation's official announcements. This page publishes only confirmed official information, so any visiting details not yet finalized will be communicated through official channels."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does Robot Park mean for Galaxy Corporation's business?",
