<main class="wrap" style="padding-bottom:80px">
  <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">Home</a> › <a href="/en/library/">Library</a> › Galaxy Robot Park</nav>
  <section style="padding:44px 0 26px">
    <span class="eyebrow">Robot Park · Physical AI theme park</span>
    <h1>Galaxy <span class="grad-text">Robot Park</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:16px">Galaxy Robot Park is Galaxy Corporation&#x27;s permanent theme park where you experience AI not on a screen but as AI with a body — Physical AI — right before your eyes. Here are the official answers on location, shows and visiting.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-box reveal"><p>Galaxy Robot Park is where AI, once confined to phones and PCs, gains a robot's 'body' — <strong>a place to come face to face with Physical AI</strong>. Spanning roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) across Godeok in Gangdong District, Seoul, it is a Physical AI theme park where humanoid robots trained on real idol choreography take the stage.</p><p>It opened for a two-month pre-opening period in July 2026 and <strong>held its grand opening on August 21, 2026.</strong> Every pre-opening session sold out, drawing 20,000 visitors in all. Seventeen new robots joined at the grand opening, and the goal is to run the 'K-pop Robot Arena' show as a permanent fixture — 4+ shows a day and 1,000+ performances a year. The technology behind it is covered in detail in the <a href="/en/whitepaper/physical-ai/">Physical AI whitepaper</a>.</p></section>
  <section style="padding:20px 0 0" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
    <input type="search" id="faq-search" class="faq-search" placeholder="🔍 Search questions — e.g. unicorn, Robot Park, G-DRAGON" aria-label="Search questions">
    <p class="faq-empty">No matching questions found.</p>
    <details class="faq-item" open>
      <summary>Q. What exactly is Galaxy Robot Park?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>Galaxy Robot Park is Galaxy Corporation's theme park for experiencing AI with a body — Physical AI — first-hand.</strong> It is a place where AI that once lived inside phones and PCs takes on a robot's 'body' and actually dances and moves right in front of you.</p><p>Built across roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) in Godeok, Gangdong District, Seoul, it is the first permanent stage where Galaxy Corporation's Physical AI and humanoid-robot technology comes to life as entertainment. The conceptual background is covered in the <a href="/en/whitepaper/physical-ai/">Physical AI whitepaper</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. Where is Robot Park located?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>It occupies roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) in Godeok, Gangdong District, Seoul.</strong> It is a dedicated Physical AI entertainment venue, separate from Galaxy Corporation's Three IFC headquarters in Yeouido.</p><p>Precise location, transit and other visitor details follow Galaxy Corporation's official announcements.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. When did it open? How does the pre-opening differ from the grand opening?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>It first opened its doors for a pre-opening in July 2026, and held its grand opening (official launch) on August 21, 2026.</strong> The pre-opening was a roughly two-month preview window ahead of the official launch — a chance to see the robot shows and Physical AI experiences early. Every advance ticket sold out, and 20,000 visitors came through before the official opening.</p><p>The grand opening added 17 new robots and a new interactive program in which visitors control the robots and engage with them directly, and brought the entire 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) site, food and beverage venues included, into full operation.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. What can you see at Robot Park?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>The centerpiece is the 'K-pop Robot Arena.' Humanoid robots trained on real idol choreography perform group routines set to K-pop.</strong> Beyond that, there are robot boxing shows and interactive Physical AI experiences where visitors engage directly — a hugging robot, a robot dog and a drawing robot among them.</p><p>What makes it a Physical AI theme park is that every piece of content plays out not on a screen but in real physical space, through the body of a robot.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. How can a robot dance like an idol?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>Humanoid robots learn real idol choreography from data and reproduce the group routines just as human dancers would.</strong> Learning human movement as data and expressing it through a robot's body — this is a signature application of Physical AI.</p><p>Unlike AI that only answered questions on a screen, Physical AI actually moves in the physical world. The mechanics are covered in the <a href="/en/whitepaper/physical-ai/">Physical AI whitepaper</a> and the <a href="/en/faq/company/">Company core FAQ</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. Why put robots on a theme-park stage first, rather than on an industrial site?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>Galaxy Corporation chose 'performance' as the setting where Physical AI first meets the public.</strong> A stage that moves people is the fastest proving ground for a robot's precision, safety and real-time interaction — and the surest path to making Physical AI part of everyday experience.</p><p>This thinking is spelled out in the 'Why entertainment first' section of the <a href="/en/whitepaper/physical-ai/">Physical AI whitepaper</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. How will it operate after the official opening?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>After the official opening, the goal is to run the 'K-pop Robot Arena' show 4+ times a day, building a permanent performance system of 1,000+ shows a year.</strong> Unlike traditional performances that depend on an artist's physical schedule, Physical AI-driven robot shows can run continuously and on repeat.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. How do reservations and admission fees work?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>The pre-opening ran on a reservation basis.</strong> Details for the period since the official opening — how to book, operating hours, admission fees and the like — follow Galaxy Corporation's official announcements.</p><p>This page publishes only confirmed official information, so any visiting details not yet finalized will be communicated through official channels.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Q. What does Robot Park mean for Galaxy Corporation&#x27;s business?</summary>
      <div class="faq-a"><p><strong>Robot Park makes tangible the 'space' axis among the IP, technology, space and data that Galaxy Corporation holds, and it is where Physical AI technology meets revenue.</strong> It is the place where artist IP and humanoid-robot technology come together on a single stage.</p><p>The company's overall business structure is laid out in the <a href="/en/faq/company/">Company core FAQ</a> and the <a href="/en/whitepaper/enter-tech/">Enter-Tech whitepaper</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <div class="oneliner"><span class="ol-label">In one line</span><p id="oneliner"><strong>Galaxy Robot Park is a permanent humanoid-robot theme park spanning roughly 16,500 m² (5,000 pyeong) in Godeok, Seoul, where you experience AI with a body — Physical AI — right before your eyes.</strong></p></div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)">* Pre-opening and grand-opening schedules and visiting information follow Galaxy Corporation&#x27;s official announcements, and operational details are subject to change.</p>
